// @error is a compiler intrinsic and cannot be redefined
// The bulk pair are emitter-intercepted from the day they were declared, so a user
// definition of one of the names is reserved — the same rule the other eighteen
// lowered memory intrinsics follow. The emitter rewrites the CALL SITE to
// `memory.fill` before any declaration is looked up, so this body would never run;
// VL rejects the DEFINITION, where the author can see it.
//
// Like the narrow store widths and unlike `__store_f64__`, these were declared and
// lowered in the same change, so there was never a shadowing hatch to close.
function __memory_fill__(d: i32, b: i32, n: i32) {
  0
}
__memory_fill__(0, 1, 1)
print(1)
